<DocsExample TExample="LayoutShellExample" Title="Header, body and footer" Description="NTLayout stacks NTHeader, NTBody and NTFooter. A layout normally fills the viewport (min-block-size: 100dvh), so this preview gives it a bounded box and overrides the block size with an inline style. In an app, leave the style off." />
<DocsExample TExample="LayoutRegionsExample" Title="Region options" Description="Tag chooses the semantic element, BackgroundColor and TextColor retheme a region, FixedPosition=false lets the header and footer scroll with the page, and RoundedCorners=false squares the body." />
<DocsExample TExample="LayoutNavigationRailExample" Title="With a navigation rail" Description="Place an NTNavigationRail as a direct child of the layout to get a rail-and-content shell. The rail is sticky and viewport-tall by default, so the preview bounds it with a fixed-height box and an inline block-size override. Items use in-page hrefs so clicking does not leave the docs." />
<DocsExample TExample="LayoutNestedExample" Title="Nested layouts" Description="A layout inside another layout becomes nested and fills the remaining space, so an inner header and body can sit inside an outer body region." />
